{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550703-the-destruction-of-the-tremere","id":1550703,"title":"The destruction of the Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-05T12:53:55-07:00","id":1550703,"title":"The destruction of the Tremere","content":"So I have been rereading the revised clanbooks lately, and I came upon a passage in the Assamite clanbook. It stated that if the sorcerers had spent more time training for combat/with weapons of the world they might have been able to wipe out all of the Tremere by now instead of spending so much time on the ladder of heaven trying to break the Tremere curse (obviously before Ur-shulgi woke up and put the wammy on the world.) My actual question is could it have happened? Could the assamites or more likely the tzimisce/gangrel/nosferatu have come together and just said &quot;fuck it&quot; and wipe out all of the Tremere? I know thaumaturgy is powerful (hence the powergamer mindset around playing them at tables), but they are not a massive clan, nor do they have easy ways to survive when faced with lots of agg, which the gangrel, assamites, and tzimisce can throw out in waves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T14:14:48-07:00","id":1550708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carsusbloodking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550703-the-destruction-of-the-tremere#post1550703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have been rereading the revised clanbooks lately, and I came upon a passage in the Assamite clanbook. It stated that if the sorcerers had spent more time training for combat/with weapons of the world they might have been able to wipe out all of the Tremere by now instead of spending so much time on the ladder of heaven trying to break the Tremere curse (obviously before Ur-shulgi woke up and put the wammy on the world.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds very much like Warrior Caste bullshit.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Sorcerers are far more powerful than the Warriors on their own.<br /> <br /> OTOH, I do actually like the fact that the Tremere Chantry in Vienna was defeated by modern weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-06-2025, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T22:22:18-07:00","id":1550722,"title":"","content":"I doubt it Carusbloodking as it would be unlikely that these clans would put aside there dislike for each other to wipeout the Tremere. It's mostly just the Warrior Caste beating there chests and looking down on the mystics who fight and think differently then them. <br /> <br /> It's a hard lesson that they sometimes needed to reminded of. For instance in the ancient past the Banu Haqim tried to kill a still mortal Ashrad and he took them out without breaking a sweat or getting a cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T22:55:38-07:00","id":1550724,"title":"","content":"Hard to tell<br /> The Tremere had insane plot armour<br /> When House Tremere became &quot;Clan&quot; Tremere - or a Tzimisce bloodline Tremere, really the other Mage Houses were not very happy either and they had their fair share of enemies on that side too <br /> The Tzimisce while not united were a formidable foes who individually or on clan level held their own against a whole Tribe of Garou, the Shadow Lord and basically anyone else who not bowed their head to them and gave them respect they demanded, not to mention had their own potent magic<br /> When they anatgonized the Gangrel and the Nosferatu - the Nosferatu, the Eyes of the Domains (basically they were like today, a close knit &quot;low Clan&quot; but they similarly traded information, they knew everything and had the means to deliver messages, vie their animals , the Nosferatu network basically had monopoly to currier service; if you wanted to make sure you are updated what the hell is going in the world you turned to them, and back in the Dark Ages this kind of reliablility was unique and essential. Literally intel and sending a message to the right person could have changed the outcome of the war. Humans had runners, currier pigeuons and so on, the Nosferatu did it better, they were the unliving mail) with the Gargoyle they basically signed their death sentence<br /> They have stollen &quot;immortality&quot;, came up with a very new blood magic in a world where already been one and more ancient form of that kind of magic and even slandered the Salubri - even if you accept no one liked the holier then thou Salubri, they kept the human healthy, like the Nosferatu newletter monopoly to medicine and healing in the Dark Ages...? Yeah, you get the picture<br /> And the Salubri had quite a few allies and friends<br /> It really not made sense to begin with the Tremere survived even if a few weaseled their way in to the courts of Princes, they essentially were Baali-light in other's eyes and a VERY dangerous precedent, mortals who tried to replace the Children of Caine...<br /> The Diablerie of Saulot not really helped... back then the Antediluvians were very active, part of the life in many Clans's cases and it wason't jus ta rumor, they boasted what they did...?<br /> The Clans united for far less in the past...<br /> So what the Warriors said?<br /> Perhaps was a bit of an exaggeration, but a fresh clan souranded by enemies in a very bad situation without any meaningful power - yeah, I can see eventually they would managed to exterminate them<br /> I mean history proved it is possible to off a whole bloodline or clan, case in point the Salubri and later the Cappadocian and they were at least valuable assets, the Tremere were simply just an offense against everything that is unholly <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T05:56:12-07:00","id":1550736,"title":"","content":"The Tremere survived because they used their rigid hierarchy, power, and alliances.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce were never a unified clan, a clan of powerful lords scattered across their individual domains with their young and rebellious children would not pose a total threat to the Tremere.<br /> <br /> United, the Tzimisce would be an implacable enemy to the Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel were never a unified clan, just like the Tzimisce. Worse still, they had no influence, domains, or troops to support them. Lethal individually, yes, but as a clan they could not cause much damage to the Tremere clan as a whole.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu were never a clan of warriors, but of spies. Their position as a Low Clan, their lack of resources, domains, and human servants in positions of influence put the clan at a clear disadvantage against the Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Assamites are indeed a threat. I believe that the clan as a whole, if they had declared an all-out war against the Tremere in the Dark Ages, would probably be the most successful faction in exterminating the Tremere. However, this would not be possible for a simple reason: the Assamites were spread across Europe, fulfilling contracts from elders and addicted to Diablerie. Their focus at the time was to commit as much Amaranth as possible. It is quite likely that for a long time they believed themselves to be proudly invincible against the other Cainites, which proved to be a mistake.<br /> <br /> The Salubri were not always divided. During the period when the Tremere clan systematically hunted the Salubri, they were separated. The vigilante caste and the healer caste would be no match for a Tremere hunting party, with access to thaumaturgy, armed minions, and the organization of the clan. It was likely that the Salubri caste of unified warriors who were once led by Samiel and fought in the Baali Wars would defeat the Tremere. However, the Salubri pogrom occurred well after the height of the Salubri warrior caste. Ahab's betrayal, combined with these factors, the Salubri propaganda about controlling the souls of other Cainites, and the likely envy of the integrity that the Salubri possessed only led to the destruction of the clan.<br /> <br /> The Tremere in general had powerful advantages, their unified clan structure is probably their greatest advantage against all other clans, Thaumaturgy is by far the most powerful and versatile discipline, a political and decisive factor for the survival of the Tremere and also their alliance with the Ventrue, amidst the chaos of the Anarch Revolt almost all clans were more concerned with their own survival than unifying a clan and fighting the Tremere, for whatever reason, the Tremere were lucky in this aspect, the alliance with a more powerful and more influential High Clan in the Dark Ages allowed the Tremere to assume a secure position as advisors to kings, being side by side with the other 6 clans during the formation of the Camarilla and the Curse on the Assamites cemented the Tremere's position of influence and power. Finally, to me it seems simply unlikely that any technology could simply destroy the Vienna Chapel, the Technomancy Line already existed making a technological attack on this scale unlikely, even focusing on the V5 rules it seems that the authors ignore the very rules they created to justify their bad scripts, Auspicius 2's Precognition was inactive in the entire clan when they were attacked, it simply doesn't make sense, maybe the building could be destroyed, but eliminating the entire clan leadership in a single attack is one of the most idiotic things I've ever read from Vampire the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T09:46:05-07:00","id":1550743,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that the Tremere's destruction of their central chantry and loss of most of the leadership will be explained away as some sort of move of Saluot who decided that his plans using the Tremere in big way was a failure and culled his clan to force a change of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T11:15:56-07:00","id":1550746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550703-the-destruction-of-the-tremere?p=1550743#post1550743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that the Tremere's destruction of their central chantry and loss of most of the leadership will be explained away as some sort of move of Saluot who decided that his plans using the Tremere in big way was a failure and culled his clan to force a change of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 Lore is a bad joke man, no one explain nothing now or in the future about this shit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T22:10:07-07:00","id":1550784,"title":"","content":"It could be something even simpler. What if the Tremere's leadership got arrogant and complacent and didn't keep up with the security protocols and they paid the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T10:21:24-07:00","id":1550797,"title":"","content":"Hard to buy, arrogant? yes, but complacent? i dont know, Inteligence is core trait of this imortal fucking mages, Etrius is live since 1022, all Seven elders complacent too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T14:09:09-07:00","id":1550813,"title":"","content":"I can buy it as much the Inner Circle of the Tremere leadership putting on a united front for the rank and file and the other clans. I can see them being distracted by petty conflicts that took away attention on security and ignoring reports from there agents out in the field. We see that in the real world.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle being so insular that clan members like Aisling Sturbridge made them nervous as she was very independent and was willing to make friends with members of the other clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T20:41:06-07:00","id":1550896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550703-the-destruction-of-the-tremere?p=1550724#post1550724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to tell<br /> The Tremere had insane plot armour</div> </div> </div> </div>Good one.<br /> Being the (alleged) PC of the creator of the game gives you that kind of power over others.<br /> <br /> The cemented strategic alliances around the world to survive against a well structured clan like the Assamites. How they survived their young years is greatly told in the Dark Ages novels. Having the Patricians on their side aided them a lot during the dark ages.<br /> <br /> - Saga<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T12:22:42-07:00","id":1550910,"title":"","content":"To be fair if you want the Tremere clan back to full strength and it's leadership and main chantry intact. There's nothing stopping you at all as most of us on this board have taken creative liberties with the metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T17:24:12-07:00","id":1550925,"title":"","content":"Your answer from the Assamite POV is on pg 42-43 of the same book. Its suggested in the time between the laying of the Tremere Curse and the rise of Ur-Shulgi and his breaking the Assamite Sorcerors were as it says &quot;a fugue.&quot;<br /> <br /> This hints at possibilities such as, the curse only worked because Ur-Shulgi / Haqim allowed it as some sort of punishment, or Ur-Shulgi was hampering the breaking as some sort of jyhadist power move to internally take over the Assamites.<br /> <br /> Needless to say a whole cast not working at 100% capacity would hamper any of the clans.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy isn't terribly powerful on its own vs what the other clans can muster, and besides nearly every clan has powerful Blood Magic users. What made the Tremere unique and powerful, was that they could siphon the strength of the entire clan at once in its rituals. Tremere and the Inner Circle can call on power from every member of their brood and use it to power their effects, which was the whole point of the Pyramid organization. The Clan structure itself was designed as a big ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}